      ],
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 180,
          "metadata": {
            "interface": true,
            "structural": true,
            "role": "content.root"
          }
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "release-entry-class",
          "nodeId": "release-entry"
        },
        "markdown": "Release Entry captures unresolved issues that block clarity.\n\nAuthored fields: `label`, `body`, `status`, `owner`, `resolutionPath`, `prominence`.\n\nThe detail surface represents the full editor contract; card and icon surfaces are deliberate projections.",
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "Release Entry is one change in a release, written for a customer.\n\n**Public fields** (copied into the release graph and drawn on the page): `title`, `category` (`new`, `changed` or `fixed`), `summary`, `detail` and `ref`. A public entry carries no commit link and no review state.\n\n**Private record**, `review` (kept in the review queue, never published): `status`, `deployStatus`, `sourceCommits`, `candidateKey`, `note`, `reviewedAt` and `releasedIn`. The form edits `status`, `deployStatus`, `note` and `reviewedAt`. `sourceCommits`, `candidateKey` and `releasedIn` are kept by the daily reviewer and the publish step.\n\n`review.status` is `pending-review`, `approved`, `deferred`, `excluded` or `published`. An entry is approved only when `deployStatus` is `verified` or `not-applicable`. Editing an approved entry sets it back to `pending-review`. Only the publish step sets `published`, and a published entry is not edited.\n\nThe card shows a status chip while it has a review record, and none once it has been published into a release graph."
        },
        "renderShape": {
          "kind": "markdown"
        }
      }
    },
